This example demonstrates why checking only the overall average
can be risky.

Overall Score      = 29.5
Hallucination Score = 85

If the system checks only:

overall_drift_score > 40

the response could incorrectly pass.

A safer approach is to check:
1. Overall drift threshold
2. Individual critical dimensions


Example:

alert = (
    overall_drift_score > 40
    or hallucination_score > 70
)


This prevents a severe problem in one dimension from being hidden
by lower scores in other dimensions.


