25. INPUT VALIDATION VS DRIFT DETECTION PARALLELISM
======================================================================

Input validation and drift detection normally belong to different
stages.


Input Validation
      |
      v
Main Task Agent
      |
      v
Response Generated
      |
      v
Drift Detection


Therefore, they normally cannot run completely in parallel for the
same request.

Reason:

The Drift Detector requires the Main Task Agent's generated response.

However, independent checks within the same stage may potentially
be executed in parallel depending on the implementation.


